From 06b3e50fe001259655284cf92cf8bc3458902781 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:44:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ::wipebank, for the administrator who has to empty a test
 bank

Dispatches in the staffModLevel >= 3 block next to ::bank and runs
content's [proc,bank_wipe] with protected access - inv_clear on the bank inv
is "$inv requires protected access" without it. The bank semantics stay in
content, where the tab counts are maintained.

Administrator rather than a debugproc because debugprocs are owner-only on a
live world, so ::~clearinv bank left an administrator on live with no way to
do this at all.

closeModal first, like ::home. The bank window is a main modal, so it makes
canAccess false - without this the command would have answered "please
finish what you are doing" to somebody looking at the bank they want
emptied, which is exactly when it gets typed. Closing it also runs
[if_close,bank_main], so the grid is unbound before anything is deleted out
from under it, and it leaves the chatbox free for the confirm.

tools/sim/wipebank.ts asserts the parts that stop a wipe happening by
accident: a moderator cannot tell the command from one that does not exist,
No leaves every item and every tab count alone, a bank PIN is not
sidestepped, and it works with the bank window open.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EKDdZD7D7Wsd9k7m6kEbjU
